1. Nf3 {[%eval +0.10] Why did I lose this game? because I completely underestimated him becauswe he was a kid. I went into the round telling myself, "great I've guaranteed myself a 4/4 finish and probably a good amount of prize money". I tried to force an advantage without calculating properly, choosing a "thematic" move and it completely backfired. I had 1 chance in the endgame to hold a draw with a fortress but missed it and my disciplined candidate move expansion went out the window towards the end. A very painful loss for me but a much needed lesson - treat every opponent like they're stockfish, because you never know how good they actually are. Everygame that I bleed half points to/lose is because I don't take the opponent seriously enough. } c6 {[%eval +0.28] } 2. d4 {[%eval +0.14] } d5 {[%eval +0.20] } 3. c4 {[%eval +0.20] } Nf6 {[%eval +0.24] } 4. e3 {[%eval +0.15] } e6 {[%eval +0.23] } 5. b3 {[%eval +0.32] } Be7 {[%eval +0.38] } 6. Bd3 {[%eval +0.30] } Nbd7 {[%eval +0.38] } 7. O-O {[%eval +0.37] } O-O {[%eval +0.42] } 8. Qc2 {[%eval +0.31] }  (8. Qe2!  ) h6 {[%eval +0.36] } 9. Bb2 {[%eval +0.36] } b6 {[%eval +0.38] } 10. Nc3 {[%eval +0.43] } Bb7 {[%eval +0.41] } 11. Rfd1 {[%eval +0.37] } Qc7 {[%eval +0.44] } 12. Rac1 {[%eval +0.46] } Rac8 {[%eval +0.64] } 13. Qe2 {[%eval +0.69] In the quiet variation of the slav, its better to put the queen on e2 at first so no wasted moves. dodging the rook xray and still preparing the e4 break, as well as not obstructing the bishop from sliding all the way back to b1. } Qb8 {[%eval +0.71] } 14. e4 {[%eval +0.17] I assumed this would be good for me because my pieces are all primed to be fighting in the centre and wanted to open my bishop pair up to the kingside, but after trading in the centre and c5! black successfuly equalizes, so perhaps this pawn break was a bit rushed. Better was ne4, creating a clamp. Taking is bad for black because the pawn can't really be removed. }  (14. Ne5  c5) dxe4 {[%eval +0.19] } 15. Nxe4 {[%eval +0.19] } c5 {[%eval +0.30] } 16. Nxf6+?! {[%eval +0.02] this just allows him to very comfortably equalise and force trades. "to take is a mistake" and in this case it was. }  (16. dxc5! {best was to keep the central tension and open up the scope of my b2 bishop. I'm still slightly better, but I was looking for a knockout because he's a kid. }  Nxe4 17. Bxe4 Nxc5 18. Bb1  (18. Bc2 {I needed to evaluate that this was slightly better for me, not just dead equal. My two bishops slice the board in half and I have good attacking prospects on the kingside. I avoided this because of my ego. }  )) Bxf6 {[%eval +0.03] } 17. d5?? {[%eval -1.59] Mistake. Be4 was best. This single handedly lost me the game. This is "thematic" and I was trying to force an advantage out of the opening where black had already sucessfully equalized. }  (17. Be4  Bxe4 18. Qxe4 b5 19. Ne5 Nxe5 20. dxe5 Bg5 21. f4 Be7 22. Rd7 Rc7) exd5 {[%eval -1.44] } 18. Bf5? {[%eval -2.81] Mistake. cxd5 was best. back to back mistakes. It's often the move you make after the first mistake that loses you the game. }  (18. cxd5  Bxd5 19. Bxf6  (19. Ba6 {this is what I saw in the game and thought I was getting good activity, but black can defend and stay just a pawn up. }  Bb7  (19... Bxb2  )  (19... Rce8  20. Qd2 Bxf3 21. gxf3)) Nxf6 20. Ne5) Bxb2 {[%eval -2.18] } 19. Qxb2 {[%eval -2.22] } Rcd8 {[%eval -2.28] } 20. cxd5 {[%eval -2.19] } Nf6 {[%eval -2.24] } 21. Ne5 {[%eval -2.23] } Rxd5 {[%eval -1.78] } 22. Rxd5 {[%eval -1.51] } Bxd5 {[%eval -1.64] } 23. Rd1 {[%eval -1.88] } Re8 {[%eval -1.29] }  (23... Rd8  ) 24. f4 {[%eval -1.38] } Qb7 {[%eval -1.06] } 25. Qf2 {[%eval -1.58] }  (25. Qd2  g6 26. Bd3 b5 27. h3 Qb6 28. Kh1 Rd8 29. Bc2) Be4 {[%eval -1.49] } 26. Bh3 {[%eval -1.58] } Nd5 {[%eval -1.19] } 27. Qh4?! {[%eval -1.80] Inaccuracy. g3 was best.}  (27. g3  ) Qc7 {[%eval -1.73] } 28. Bd7 {[%eval -1.66] } Rd8 {[%eval -1.93] } 29. Bc6? {[%eval -3.36] Mistake. Qe1 was best. bc6 is not good because black can force trades into a winning endgame after f6 or nf6. }  (29. Qe1 {Maybe I didn't expand my candidate moves enough as I didn't  considder this. This is a threat, so It should have been looked at in CCT checklist. It tries to remove the defender of the knight. If f5 is played, the black has permenantly weakened his kingside. }  Nf6  (29... f5  30. Be6+ Kh7 31. Nf7 Rf8 32. Bxd5 Bxd5 33. Ne5) 30. Bb5 Rxd1 31. Qxd1 Bd5 32. Bc4 Bxc4 33. bxc4 g6 34. g4 Kg7)  (29. f5  )  (29. Qg4  ) Nf6 {[%eval -3.36] }  (29... f6  ) 30. Rxd8+ {[%eval -3.38] } Qxd8 {[%eval -3.13] } 31. Bb5?! {[%eval -4.09] Inaccuracy. h3 was best.}  (31. h3  Bxc6 32. Nxc6 Qa8 33. Ne5 Qe4 34. Qf2 Nd5 35. g3 Nc3 36. Kh2 Qb1) Qd4+ {[%eval -3.35] }  (31... Qd1+  32. Bf1 Qa1 33. Qf2) 32. Qf2 {[%eval -3.33] } Qa1+ {[%eval -3.21] } 33. Bf1 {[%eval -3.04] } Bb1 {[%eval -2.89] } 34. Qd2 {[%eval -2.20] } Qd4+ {[%eval -2.24] } 35. Qxd4 {[%eval -2.16] } cxd4 {[%eval -1.84] } 36. Bc4?! {[%eval -2.80] Inaccuracy. a3 was best.}  (36. a3  Ne4 37. Ba6 Bc2 38. Kf1 Bxb3 39. Nc6 Nc5 40. Nxd4 Bd5 41. Be2 Kf8) Bxa2 {[%eval -2.63] } 37. Nc6?! {[%eval -3.40] Inaccuracy. Kf2 was best.}  (37. Kf2 {I needed to prioritise king developement first . }  Ne4+ 38. Ke2 Nc5 39. b4 Bxc4+ 40. Nxc4 Na6 41. b5 Nb4 42. Nd6 Kf8)  (37. Bxf7+ {I was actually able to just grab a pawn and then come back, though everything was just losing for me anyways. Practically, its probably best to bring my king in first to set up a defensive fortress. }  Kf8 38. Bc4) Ne4 {[%eval -3.56] } 38. Nxd4 {[%eval -3.42] } Nd2 {[%eval -3.74] } 39. Bd5 {[%eval -3.71] } a5 {[%eval -3.61] } 40. Kf2 {[%eval -3.50] } a4 {[%eval -3.13] } 41. Ke3 {[%eval -3.47] } Bxb3 {[%eval -3.12] } 42. Nxb3?! {[%eval -4.15] Inaccuracy. Bxf7+ was best.}  (42. Bxf7+  Kxf7 43. Kxd2 Be6 44. Kc3 Bd7 45. Kb4 Ke7 46. Nc2 h5 47. h3 Ke6) Nxb3 {[%eval -4.13] } 43. Kd3 {[%eval -3.83] } b5 {[%eval -3.72] } 44. Kc3 {[%eval -3.51] } Kf8 {[%eval -3.47] } 45. Bc6 {[%eval -3.58] } Nc1 {[%eval -3.44] } 46. Bxb5?! {[